#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:2
msgid "Self-Hosted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:5
msgid "Buy a subscription"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:7
msgid ""
"To purchase a commercial subscription for Mattermost Enterprise or "
"Mattermost Professional, please visit our pricing page online: "
"https://mattermost.com/pricing/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:10
msgid "Apply your license"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:12
msgid ""
"Once downloaded, your Mattermost license is ready to use and is applied "
"via the Mattermost System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:14
msgid "Apply the Mattermost Enterprise license using the System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:17
msgid ""
"System admin access is required in order to apply the license. If you're "
"not a Mattermost system admin, contact your organization's Mattermost "
"system admin for assistance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:20
msgid "Mattermost installed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:22
msgid ""
"Check your email for a purchase confirmation from Mattermost. Download "
"the attached license. In Mattermost, follow the steps provided in "
"**System Console > About > Edition and License** to apply your license "
"key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:24
msgid ""
"You can also use the :ref:`mmctl <administration-guide/manage/mmctl-"
"command-line-tool:mmctl license>` to apply the license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:27
msgid "Mattermost not yet installed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:29
msgid ""
"If you haven't yet installed and deployed a Mattermost instance, visit "
"the :doc:`Deployment Guide </deployment-guide/deployment-guide-index>` to"
" get started. For information on creating a system admin account, visit "
"our :doc:`Administrator Tasks </administration-guide/upgrade/admin-"
"onboarding-tasks>` documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:32
msgid "Add more users to your subscription"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:34
msgid ""
"If at any time you'd like to add more users to your Mattermost "
"subscription, talk to a `Mattermost Expert <https://mattermost.com"
"/contact-sales/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:37
msgid "Quarterly true-up reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:39
msgid ""
"When you buy an annual Mattermost subscription, you agree to provide "
"Mattermost with quarterly reports of the actual number of activated users"
" within your system. An activated user is a user who has a Mattermost "
"account and doesn't show as **Deactivated** in **System Console > User "
"Management > Users**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:41
msgid ""
"Single-channel guests are tracked separately from activated users. Guests"
" in exactly one channel are free up to a 1:1 ratio with licensed seats, "
"while guests in multiple channels continue to count as activated users. "
"Direct messages and group messages don't affect whether a guest is "
"counted as a single-channel guest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:43
msgid ""
"We'll send you an email notice around the end of the quarter reminding "
"you to send us your report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:45
msgid "The timeframes followed for the true-up notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:48
msgid ""
"If you have more total activated users than you purchased in your annual "
"subscription, your Customer Success Manager will provide you with a true-"
"up quote for the new users added. The additional invoice will be pro-"
"rated based on the number of months left in your subscription term, "
"including the months for the calendar quarter for the time you pull the "
"report. Mattermost won't provide downward adjustments. Mattermost will "
"invoice based on Mattermost’s `current list prices "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:50
msgid ""
"A system admin must take a screenshot of the **System Console > Reporting"
" > Site Statistics** page and send it to Mattermost in an email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:52
msgid ""
"Please ensure your screenshot is taken from the top of the page and "
"includes **Total Activated Users**, **Single-channel Guests**, and "
"**Monthly Active Users**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:53
msgid "Please include the date of the screenshot in the file name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:54
msgid ""
"We don't need your server address, so if it appears on your screenshot, "
"you can redact it from the image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:58
msgid ""
"Not sure where to take the screenshot? Please reach out to your account "
"executive, your Customer Success Manager, orders@mattermost.com, or "
"`create a support ticket <https://support.mattermost.com/hc/en-"
"us/requests/new?ticket_form_id=11184911962004>`_ for assistance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:61
msgid "Renew your subscription"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:63
msgid ""
"System admins will be alerted 60 days prior to license expiry via a "
"banner in Mattermost. You can also dismiss the banner and renew your "
"license at a later date via **System Console > Edition and License**. To "
"renew your license, talk to a `Mattermost Expert <https://mattermost.com"
"/contact-sales/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:66
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:69
msgid "What is the minimum number of users I can purchase on a subscription?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:71
msgid ""
"The minimum purchase for a Mattermost license subscription is **more than"
" 10 users** (i.e., at least 11). There is no set maximum — you can buy as"
" many user seats as your organization requires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:74
msgid "What is a true-up report and why is the true-up notice necessary?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:76
msgid ""
"A true-up report is our quarterly request for you to provide us with the "
"actual number of activated users within your system to determine if you "
"have more activated users now than when you bought your subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:78
msgid ""
"As your organization grows, you may need to add additional users during "
"your subscription period. Mattermost needs to have insight into changes "
"in your activated user count so that we can charge you appropriately for "
"your self-hosted license usage. Additionally, we don’t want to over "
"estimate/charge activated users at your renewal time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:80
msgid ""
"Single-channel guests are visible separately in reporting and on the "
"**Edition and License** page. They don't count toward the primary paid "
"seat count up to a 1:1 ratio with licensed seats, and exceeding that "
"allowance generates system-admin warnings rather than hard limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:82
msgid ""
"When you receive the quarterly true-up notice from Mattermost, please "
"share your activated user count with us."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:85
msgid "How do I renew my subscription if I don't have internet access?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:87
msgid ""
"If you don't have access to the internet, please `create a support ticket"
" <https://support.mattermost.com/hc/en-"
"us/requests/new?ticket_form_id=11184911962004>`_ for assistance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:90
msgid "Can I use my Mattermost license on more than one server?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:92
msgid ""
"Each license covers one deployment — either a single server, or multiple "
"nodes in a High Availability configuration that share a single database. "
"If you need to run a second independent server, that requires its own "
"license. Contact your account team for assistance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:95
msgid "Can I use my license in a non-production environment?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:97
msgid ""
"Non-production environments are provisioned with a dedicated license key "
"separate from the production license. Customers with Premier Support are "
"eligible for up to four non-production license keys. Customers without "
"Premier Support should contact their account team for assistance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:100
msgid "Where can I find my new license key?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:102
msgid ""
"Once your payment is successfully processed, your license key will be "
"provided via email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:105
msgid "How will I know when to renew my subscription?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:107
msgid ""
"You'll be notified 60 days prior to your subscription expiry, via a blue "
"banner displayed at the top of your Mattermost window. This banner is "
"only visible to system admins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:109
msgid ""
"You can select **Renew license now** to begin the renewal process. You "
"can also select the **x** to dismiss the notification. The notification "
"is reactivated when your browser is refreshed or you reload the "
"Mattermost Desktop App."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:112
msgid "How long does it take to renew a subscription?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:114
msgid ""
"Once you’ve started the renewal process, we'll be in contact with you to "
"confirm your order and send you the order form. There may be additional "
"paperwork required. Once we have the signed order form and (if "
"applicable) the necessary paperwork from you, we're able to process the "
"renewal and issue your license key within 24 hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:117
msgid "What happens to my subscription if I don't renew in time?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:119
msgid ""
"If you don't renew within the 60-day renewal period, a 10-day grace "
"period is provided. During this period your Mattermost installation runs "
"as normal, with full access to commercial features. During the grace "
"period, the notification banner is not dismissable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:121
msgid ""
"When the grace period expires, your Mattermost Enterprise or Professional"
" plan is downgraded to the Free plan and other plan features are "
"disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:124
msgid "What happens when my subscription expires?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:126
msgid ""
"If you don't renew within the 10-day grace period, your Mattermost "
"version is automatically downgraded to Free plan so you can still access "
"and use Mattermost. However, subscription features will no longer be "
"available, and if you are currently using them, the functionality will no"
" longer be accessible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:128
msgid ""
"When you renew, the subscription features will become available with the "
"previous configuration (provided no action such as user migration has "
"been taken)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:131
msgid "Why can't I dismiss the expiry notification banner?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:133
msgid ""
"If there's a red expiry announcement banner stating: \"Enterprise license"
" is expired and some features may be disabled. Please contact your system"
" admin for details.\" it means your grace period has expired. This "
"announcement banner persists until the license is renewed, and is visible"
" to all users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:135
msgid "Once a new license is applied, the banner will no longer be visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:137
msgid ""
"If you don't plan to renew your subscription, revoke the expired license "
"in **System Console > Edition and License**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:140
msgid "Where can I find the license agreement for Mattermost Enterprise Edition?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/self-hosted-subscriptions.rst:142
msgid ""
"Mattermost Enterprise Edition is the name for the binary of the "
"Mattermost self-hosted Enterprise and Professional editions. This edition"
" can be used for free without a license key as commercial software "
"functionally equivalent to the open source Mattermost Team Edition "
"licensed under MIT. When a license key is purchased and applied to "
"Mattermost Enterprise Edition, additional features unlock. The license "
"agreement for Mattermost Enterprise Edition is included in the software "
"and also available `here <https://mattermost.com/enterprise-edition-"
"license/>`_."
msgstr ""

